course: dictionary
lesson: 6421
title: Mutt and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. «We took our mutt to the park.» Mutt here is a dog, and the park and the word our give you the clue. A mutt is a dog of no particular breed, a mix of lots of breeds, and people often say it with love.
explain: «The scruffy mutt wagged its tail at everyone.» Scruffy means untidy, so the clues show a messy but friendly dog. Ask: what word would fit here? Dog fits, so mutt is a kind of dog. Swap in your meaning and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Mutt can also be an old-fashioned insult meaning a silly or stupid person. «Grandad said his brother was a mutt for forgetting the keys.» The forgetting shows that mutt means a silly person here, not a dog. Check the clues each time.
explain: Look for capital letters and quote marks too. In «"Mutt", to an art show, asking who decides what art is», the capital M and the quote marks show that Mutt is a name, not a dog. Context has settled it.
fact: Mutt means a dog of no particular breed, a mixed-breed dog.
fact: Mutt is informal, so you would use it in friendly talk, not in a school report.
fact: Useful phrases: «a scruffy mutt» and «a lovable mutt».
fact: As an insult, mutt means a silly or stupid person, and it is old-fashioned.
fact: In an art story, «Mutt» can be a name. An everyday object shown as art is called a readymade.
exercise: «My mutt loves chasing balls in the park.» What is a mutt? | A type of art show | A cat with stripes | A very tall tree | *A dog of no particular breed
exercise: Grandad says his brother is a mutt for being silly. What does mutt mean here? | A mixed-breed cat | A scruffy, lovable dog | *A silly or stupid person | A park with lots of trees
exercise: «"Mutt", to an art show, asking who decides what art is» What is Mutt most likely to be? | A readymade | A dog that loves art | A silly person in a park | *A name, shown by a capital M and quote marks
test: What does scruffy mean in «a scruffy mutt»? | Very big | *Untidy and messy | Quiet and shy | Very clean and shiny
test: Jayden says, «My mutt got a bath today.» What does mutt mean? | Very clean | *A mixed-breed dog | A silly person | A big house
exam: Nadia asks, «Does mutt always mean a dog?» What is the best answer? | *No: it can also be an old insult for a silly person, or a name in a story | Only in art shows, never about dogs | No, it means a big house | Yes, always, and nothing else
